<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Tuesday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>   Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*  *G*   *H*</p>
<p>Mar 04  20,623 4,965 25,588 13,372 13,386 5,544  0  18,930</p>
<p>Mar 05  20,515 4,871 25,386 13,508 13,523 5,503  0  19,026</p>
<p>Mar 06  20,421 4,945 25,366 13,700 13,715 5,295  0  19,010</p>
<p>Mar 07  20,511 4,800 25,311 13,783 13,799 5,333  0  19,132</p>
<p>Mar 10  20,467 4,726 25,193 13,770 13,798 5,326  0  19,124</p>
<p>Mar 11  20,551 4,746 25,297 13,589 13,619 5,573  0  19,192</p>
<p>Mar 12  20,563 4,773 25,336 13,468 13,497 5,708  0  19,205</p>
<p>Mar 13  20,578 4,964 25,542 13,407 13,435 5,773  0  19,208</p>
<p>Mar 14  20,614 4,958 25,572 13,360 13,391 5,857  0  19,248</p>
<p>*A  Of the $20.61 billion in international reserves, $2.37 billion (11.51 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0651))</p>
</text>
